# Consistency and Migrations

- When the codebase shows two patterns for the same thing, pick the more modern, feature-based one and move toward it – do not add more code using the older pattern.
- Standardize React context naming and placement on `*Context.tsx` files inside a `context/` folder (e.g. events context); avoid inventing new naming/location variants.
- Prefer feature-local versions of shared UI (like sidebars) over legacy versions in top-level `src/components`; new work should not introduce more legacy components.
- Normalize imports to the `@/` alias; do not introduce new deep relative paths for features or shared modules.
- When touching legacy areas, budget time to align them with these rules instead of copying old inconsistencies forward.
